+---
+date: 2026-11-13
+quest: ../QUEST.md
+exp: 6
+status: proposed
+---
+
+# Exp 6 — Hooks emission (`bp3 q hooks`)
+
+## TL;DR
+
+Implement the settled Exp 4 hooks design: a `bp3 q hooks` verb
+that reads one Muse hook event JSON from stdin, self-gates,
+resolves the witnessed Run binding, and writes past-tense event
+lines into the exp ledger through an internal fact writer.
+`bp3 skills install` delivers the project-tier
+`.muse/hooks.json` that registers it. The design contract is
+[Exp 4's adopted record](../exp-4-tape-hooks/EXPERIMENT.md);
+this exp is its implementation vehicle.
+
+Status: **proposed, not implemented.** Fails today: no `hooks`
+verb, no installed `.muse/hooks.json`, no event lines in any
+ledger.
+
+## Demo (design trace — nothing here has run yet)
+
+```text
+$ printf '%s' '{"hook_event_name":"PostLLMCall","session_id":"S1",
+  "usage":{"input_tokens":33250,"output_tokens":209,
+  "cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":119}}' | ./bin/bp3 q hooks
+{"ok":true,"event_line":null,"reason":"no binding witnessed for session"}
+
+$ # after a PreToolUse payload whose tool_input.command carries
+$ # BP3_RUN_ID=20261113T120000Z-submit-muse-code-muse-wonder-1.0-c1:
+ledger.jsonl += {"ts":"...","event":"usage_recorded","run_id":"...-c1",
+  "input_tokens":33250,"output_tokens":209,"cached_tokens":0,
+  "reasoning_tokens":119,"wall_ms":...,"started_ts":"...","settled_ts":"..."}
+```
+
+```text
+Muse hook event (stdin JSON)
+  -> bp3 q hooks
+       1. parse payload; garbage in -> exit 0, write nothing
+       2. gate: bin/bp3 + docs/quests/ at cwd root? no -> exit 0
+       3. reentrancy: payload caused by bp3 q itself? -> exit 0
+       4. PreToolUse with BP3_RUN_ID in tool_input.command?
+          record session_id -> run_id in the run registry
+       5. resolve binding; unbound -> exit 0, write nothing
+       6. map event -> past-tense kind; aggregate PostLLMCall usage
+       7. fact writer appends the event line (no edge/from/to),
+          dedupe by run_id + kind
+```
+
+```python
+def bp3_q_hooks(payload: dict) -> int:  # always exits 0
+    if not is_bp3_repo(cwd) or reentrant(payload): return 0
+    if payload.event == "PreToolUse" and (m := ENV_PRESET.search(payload.command)):
+        registry.bind(payload.session_id, m.run_id); write("run_started", ...)
+    run = registry.resolve(payload.session_id)
+    if run is None: return 0
+    kind = KIND_BY_EVENT[payload.event]  # past tense, see table
+    if kind: fact_writer.append(run.exp_ledger, {event: kind, ts: now(), run_id: run.id, ...})
+    return 0
+```
+
+| Piece | Contract |
+|---|---|
+| Verb | `bp3 q hooks` — no positional args, one JSON object on stdin, exit 0 always (fail-open), JSON verdict on stdout |
+| Event kinds | `run_started`, `run_settled`, `run_unsettled`, `usage_recorded`, `refused`, `lint_checked` — each line has `ts`, `run_id`; never `edge`/`from`/`to` |
+| Inputs | eight events: `SessionStart`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `PostToolUseFailure`, `PostLLMCall`, `SubagentStart`, `SubagentStop`, `Stop`/`SessionEnd` |
+| Binding | env preset witnessed in `PreToolUse` `tool_input.command`; first match per session wins; unbound -> write nothing |
+| Usage | `PostLLMCall` payloads aggregated per Run; one `usage_recorded` at settle with real token fields + `wall_ms`, `started_ts`, `settled_ts` |
+| Death | `SessionStart` sweeps stale bindings -> `run_unsettled` |
+| Delivery | `bp3 skills install` also writes `.muse/hooks.json` (one command: `bp3 q hooks`) into bp3-enabled repos |
+| File changes (proposed) | `+ src/quest/hooks.ml` (verb + fact writer) · `u src/quest/main.ml` (dispatch) · `u bin/bp3` / installer (hooks.json delivery) · `+ test/hooks.sh` · `u Makefile` (wire test) |
+
+## Acceptance (fails today)
+
+| Case | Expected |
+|---|---|
+| garbage on stdin | exit 0, writes nothing |
+| hook fires outside a bp3 repo | exit 0, writes nothing |
+| unbound session event | exit 0, writes nothing |
+| bound Run | `run_started`, then `run_settled`, in the exp ledger |
+| Run ends | exactly one `usage_recorded`, real `PostLLMCall` fields |
+| session killed mid-Run | `run_unsettled` at next `SessionStart` |
+| refused `bp3 q u` observed | `refused` {code, attempted edge}; state unchanged |
+| lint exit witnessed | `lint_checked` {check, pass\|fail} |
+| parallel Runs | distinct bindings, no cross-talk, dedupe by `run_id + kind` |
+| any event line | `ts` + `run_id`, no `edge`/`from`/`to`; fold skips it |
+
+## Acceptance test (goal block)
+
+- **Objective:** implement `bp3 q hooks` + installer delivery
+  so hook events become ledger event lines per the Exp 4
+  record.
+- **Prove by:** `test/hooks.sh` piping fixture payloads
+  (garbage, foreign repo, unbound, bound, killed session,
+  refused edge) and asserting exit codes + ledger contents;
+  then one live `induct-exp` run with `.muse/hooks.json`
+  installed, reading real event lines in an exp ledger.
+- **Done when:** every Acceptance case passes, `make check`
+  is green, and no code path parses tape text into facts.
+
+## Context
+
+Exp 4 settled this design in its reopened red-ink walk
+(2026-11-13) after the landing review found the original
+hooks work had shipped unsettled. The env preset half already
+landed in `induct-exp.js` (`envPreset`, commit `3c92a70`);
+this exp builds the receiving half. Warden consumption and
+session-log mining are out of scope (icebox).
